ild --filter Name~NoFixtureSitsOnTheBaseWithoutAReason", "exit": 1}, {"command": "pwsh Lighthouse.Backend/Create-Migration.ps1 -MigrationName AddOrganisationStructure", "exit": 0}, {"command": "dotnet build Lighthouse.Backend/Lighthouse.sln", "exit": 0}, {"command": "dotnet test Lighthouse.Backend/Lighthouse.Backend.Tests --filter FullyQualifiedName~Acceptance.OneStructure.TwoLevelsFromTerminology", "exit": 0}, {"command": "dotnet test Lighthouse.Backend/Lighthouse.Backend.Tests --filter FullyQualifiedName~Acceptance.OneStructure.MappingFromUnits", "exit": 0}, {"command": "dotnet test Lighthouse.Backend/Lighthouse.Backend.Tests --filter FullyQualifiedName~Acceptance.OneStructure.NumbersStayTheSame", "exit": 0}, {"command": "dotnet test Lighthouse.Backend/Lighthouse.Backend.Tests --filter FullyQualifiedName~Architecture.OrganisationSetup", "exit": 0}, {"command": "dotnet test Lighthouse.Backend/Lighthouse.Backend.Tests --filter FullyQualifiedName~OrganisationStructurePlanPurityArchUnitTest", "exit": 0}, {"command": "dotnet test Lighthouse.Backend/Lighthouse.Backend.Tests --filter FullyQualifiedName~TestTierGuardTest", "exit": 0}, {"command": "dotnet test Lighthouse.Backend/Lighthouse.Backend.Tests --filter FullyQualifiedName~TerminologyServiceTest|FullyQualifiedName~TerminologyControllerTest|FullyQualifiedName~TerminologyControllerAuthorizationTests", "exit": 0}, {"command": "pwsh Lighthouse.Backend/Test-Fast.ps1", "exit": 0}], "outcome": "accepted", "diagnostic": "S2 is GREEN on the revised oracle; this is rework round 2. Results: TwoLevelsFromTerminology 14/14 on SQLite and Postgres. MappingFromUnits 6/6. S1 NumbersStayTheSame 2/2. Architecture.OrganisationSetup 119/119. OrganisationStructurePlanPurityArchUnitTest 2/2. TestTierGuardTest 90/90 (the oracle's move to Tests.Integration.Containers fixed the earlier guard finding). Terminology service, controller and authorization tests 14/14. Test-Fast.ps1, with its build, 12758/12758. dotnet build Lighthouse.sln: 0 warnings, 0 errors.\n\nThe only change in round 2 is TerminologyService.GetAll. Each row now keeps its stored Value and DefaultValue, as it did before the upgrade. For the eight level words, a non-empty stored Value is answered from the level. An empty Value stays empty, because empty means \"use the default word\". The level always holds the word in use. PUT /terminology writes the raw value to the row and writes the word in use (the value, or the default when it is empty) to the level. The rows are dual-written, so rows and levels cannot drift apart.\n\nUnchanged from round 1:\n- Migration AddOrganisationStructure, generated by Create-Migration.ps1: SQLite 20261128175242, Postgres 20261128175250. It creates four tables and alters or drops nothing.\n- TerminologyService takes an optional IOrganisationStructureStore, because S1's immutable UnitNumbersRecorder registers Terminology without the levels. Open bypass: a composition that leaves out AddOrganisationStructure does not reach the levels.\n- GetAll blocks on Load, because its port is synchronous.\n- The EF records are in Adapters/Persistence. The structure uses fixed key 1 and a concurrency token, and a racing loser re-reads.\n- ConnectionMapping gains MappedLevels, WithCreateDefaults(connection) and UsesItemTypes. Defaults come from new Team() and new Portfolio().\n- If the migrator's self-check fails, it throws WHAT/WHY/HOW and rolls back. That failure path is untested.\n- HistoricalSchemaPatch is unchanged. It patches only columns of tables that the fixtures seed, and the new tables are never seeded. All four of its callers pass. A reviewer should confirm this reading of \"learns the new tables\".\n- The purity test uses IL dependencies against EF, Data, API, Adapters, IO, Net, logging, ILighthouseClock, DateTime, DateTimeOffset, TimeProvider and Random. Its second test shows that the same rule catches the migrator.\n\nNo refactor commits. Jev was refused (unauthorized) and was not asked. Test-writing skill read in full and fresh: \"End of SKILL.md\" / \"End of backend.md\". Not run: the full filtered dotnet test (the Program.cs edit requires the full Integration suite) and Stryker.\n", "blocked_by": null, "slice": "S2"}
